[{:db/id "q-166218/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b3c1dd50-e591-5613-af40-d7e93107918e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-166218/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6feff4d0-fd8f-5dbe-88e1-8b146ccab997" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-166218/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-166218/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-166218" :question/id #uuid "3780e331-ad54-57c9-a1d3-183beea2fe73" :question/math-academy-id "q-166218" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ is given by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(2)={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2}=-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x\\,+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Simplifying the expression under the limit, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(2) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{[4-{x}^{2}]-[4-{2}^{2}]}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{4-{x}^{2}}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{-({x}^{2}-4)}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{-(x+2)(x-2)}{x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{-(x+2)\\cancel{(x-2)}}{\\cancel{x-2}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-166218/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8f2e684-6cd8-5ede-9f70-1a24ada54cb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-166218"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-166217/field-1/9cdabb2882bf00c7a5859de6ff52cc4fd4bada5dbb73f9b5dc5f04c34bb7b0c5" :answer/id #uuid "58d9e57e-f446-5415-8893-879950cf8d7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-166217/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ad08d2e-4cb8-52a6-b31d-060fd0512bde" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-166217/field-1/9cdabb2882bf00c7a5859de6ff52cc4fd4bada5dbb73f9b5dc5f04c34bb7b0c5" :answer-field/choices ["q-166217/field-1/9cdabb2882bf00c7a5859de6ff52cc4fd4bada5dbb73f9b5dc5f04c34bb7b0c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-166217" :question/id #uuid "386145e1-97c4-5291-9ae5-69c49e55606b" :question/math-academy-id "q-166217" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit directly by substituting $x=2,$ we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{4-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}}{4-{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since there is a radical in the numerator, we can evaluate the limit by first multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{4-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{(\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x})(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})}{(4-{x}^{2})(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{2-x}{(2+x)(2-x)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\cancel{2-x}}{(2+x)\\cancel{(2-x)}(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{1}{(2+x)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(2+2)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4(2\\sqrt{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-166217/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-166217"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-166220/field-1/412793739940b973be2b527fb17aec02d6ca6345201ec8cd477bb75bb5283b50" :answer/id #uuid "94dd5fb0-d678-5d32-896d-1021b98814e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-166220/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a46f348-6137-5ac0-b013-1d7682ea2b82" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-166220/field-1/412793739940b973be2b527fb17aec02d6ca6345201ec8cd477bb75bb5283b50" :answer-field/choices ["q-166220/field-1/412793739940b973be2b527fb17aec02d6ca6345201ec8cd477bb75bb5283b50"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-166220" :question/id #uuid "1a63e24a-e04b-5db9-bbc1-e9ee3edfd2ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-166220" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ is given by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(2)={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2}=-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x\\,+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$).$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\n$-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\,(x+2)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe derivative of $f(x)$ is defined by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$-\\,h\\,).$" :question/worked-solution "Simplifying the expression under the limit, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{4-(x+h)^{2}-[4-{x}^{2}]}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{4-{x}^{2}-2xh-{h}^{2}-4+{x}^{2}}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{-2xh-{h}^{2}}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{h(-2x-h)}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{\\cancel{h}(-2x-h)}{\\cancel{h}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}(-2x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-166220/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c6f3c71-d11b-59af-bad6-5f5c0ff6634f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-166220"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-166223/field-1/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer/id #uuid "746029fa-3599-590c-9f99-c62801f49b2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-166223/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e32efa9-400e-593e-9b27-f5ce542becbe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-166223/field-1/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer-field/choices ["q-166223/field-1/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-166223" :question/id #uuid "3d9d3fe9-2259-5414-99ae-3627c722db65" :question/math-academy-id "q-166223" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ is given by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(2)={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\frac{f(x)-f(2)}{x-2}=-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x\\,+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$).$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\n$-{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}\\,(x+2)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nThe derivative of $f(x)$ is defined by\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2x$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$-\\,h\\,).$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\n${f}^{′}(x)={lim}_{h\\to \\,0}(-2x-h)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2x$\n\nEarlier part 7:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950896/assets/19d0c50eff5613451c833c00e2d151b93ca5d7e490366fc811d6730e383227de.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above (not drawn to scale). Estimate the area $A$ using a right Riemann sum with step size $Δx=0.5.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,≈\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4.25$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nWrite the expression for the Riemann sum from part 7 in sigma notation.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The right Riemann sum $\\,=\\,0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4-$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         ${i}^{2})$" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nIn our case, we have $n=4$ subintervals, $a=0,$ $b=2,$ and $Δx=0.5.$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(0+i\\cdot 0.5)\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(0.5i) \\\\  & =0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4-{(0.5i)}^{2}) \\\\  & =0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4-0.25{i}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-166223/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-166223"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-166224/field-1/5b67963ce634a64b841a125a1784f0c5be44ed2f2d7ab645cafeab811a9a9443" :answer/id #uuid "a1169cd4-fbef-58a1-80ad-0edfa1889e30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4-x^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-166224/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "10c24635-fa09-554e-870b-16082908843f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-166224/field-1/5b67963ce634a64b841a125a1784f0c5be44ed2f2d7ab645cafeab811a9a9443" :answer-field/choices ["q-166224/field-1/5b67963ce634a64b841a125a1784f0c5be44ed2f2d7ab645cafeab811a9a9443"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-166224/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "c2fb2e94-7aa0-50c4-8ea4-deb961cfbca8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [